      "reason": "Optional per-part `cut: \"late\"` for an interrupted sentence whose previous word ends in a stop consonant released into the next word (p348 \"accused of\"). The default cut is the quietest point = the stop closure, which left the release burst at the start of the second part (heard as \"the returning\"); \"late\" cuts after the burst, before the next word's vowel (2 ms window, latest point under 25% of median speech level). Without `cut` the behaviour is unchanged. segments.mjs validates / passes the field, split.mjs implements it.",
