      "reason": "Series identity and the content-emoji default (P4 onward). (1) Structured series metadata on an episode: `series` (the vocabulary library), `seriesEpisode` (explicit positive integer: which video of that series), `level: { min, max }` (1–3, min <= max) and `contentId` (the source content id; informational). None of them is derived from contentId, the file name or the folder. (2) New header rendering path (reference/Header.js, used by PostTemplate.js): the top right shows `series · #NN · level` (1 → #01, 100 → #100; min === max → L2, otherwise L1–L2 with an en dash, a display form that is not stored). (3) On that path the account row's level badge is not drawn (the level must not appear twice) and `episodeLabel` / `author.level` are not required (a warning if present). (4) Legacy episodes (no `series`: P2, P3) take exactly the old path: `episodeLabel` in the top right and the level badge in the account row; their frozen episode files are not touched. (5) Content emoji default = off: for an episode that uses the structured metadata, episode-refs.mjs reports an error for a decorative emoji in the hook, story, vocabulary, quiz, outro, status, social / outside or in a narration line (explicit exception: `allowContentEmoji: true`; the account avatar, the brand mascot and UI glyphs are not content); verify-episode.mjs also checks the rendered text. A scene_contrast hook no longer needs `emoji` (Components.js draws none when it is absent; number_contrast still requires it). verify-episode.mjs adds a header check (shown text, level shown once, fits next to the brand). The rule and the series table are written into docs/video-design-system.md. ReadingCue.js is unchanged.",
